{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Take, the one who blesses</b> — [verses 13–14] two joined: the one who blesses his friend is he who stood surety for a stranger, and who blesses his friend the lender in a loud voice, so that others may hear the blessing and find favor in his eyes, so that he will not take his garment. In the morning he rises early for his work and blesses him, and his friend the blesser reckons it as though he cursed him, and he will not spare [him] from taking his garment."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:03.029056237Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}